{"base_rate":0.35278514588859416,"brier":0.16615994694960212,"bss":0.2722745254529767,"bss_hi":0.35987496553586695,"bss_lo":0.16273939168115245,"chart":{"base":[519.4,158.9],"fp":[270.9,221.4],"lead":"62,272.3 272,243.7 482,205.8 692,137.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 34% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +22pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 87% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 8%; promised 100% → rained 81%"},"rel":"67.3,430.2 212.8,361 543.7,245.6 690.2,114.5"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1297612732095491,"ess":469.3188217023192,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Melbourne</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Melbourne rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 754 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMELBOURNE BOTANICAL GARDENS, 2.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 88 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(53&ndash;112) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>302</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>161</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Melbourne</b> <span class=\"muted\">AU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>53&ndash;112\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>754 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Melbourne &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Melbourne\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=